<p><strong>In this post, I will explain my reasoning and results of a multilevel analysis.</strong></p>
<hr>
<p>Context:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>300 participants with hyper sexuality problems.</p></li>
<li><p>Participants where measured weekly over the span of 9 weeks.</p></li>
<li><p>dependent variable: psychological wellbeing.</p></li>
</ul>
<p>Visualization of research design:</p>
<div class="quarto-figure quarto-figure-center">
<figure class="figure">
<p><img src="images/geneste niveaus.png" class="img-fluid figure-img" width="602"></p>
<figcaption>Nested measurements within participants.</figcaption>
</figure>
</div>
<p>Research question:</p>
<div class="callout callout-style-default callout-important no-icon callout-titled">
<div class="callout-header d-flex align-content-center">
<div class="callout-icon-container">
<i class="callout-icon no-icon"></i>
</div>
<div class="callout-title-container flex-fill">
Important
</div>
</div>
<div class="callout-body-container callout-body">
<p><em>What is the longitudinal effect of therapy and/or medication on psychological wellbeing on participants with hyper sexuality complaints.</em></p>
</div>
</div>
<hr>
